Pokemon scarlet and violets are out now  and the reception to both highly  anticipated titles has been mixed to say  the least multiple reviews including our  own Gamespot mentioned that while the  open world is an excellent step forward  for the franchise the games are held  back by technical issues such as pop-in  frame rate drops and muddy textures as  such the current score at Gamespot  sister site Metacritic sits at a 77  which is the lowest score for a new  Mainline Pokemon game ever before these  entries no new generation of Pokemon has  scored below an 80 before I should note  that neither Pokemon red blue or gold  silver have ratings on the site but  their remakes fire red leaf green and  heart gold soul silver are also rated  highly which of course they are because  those are some of the greatest games of  all time despite the mixed reception to  the new games it seems to not have had  any effect on sale as college and  violets are the most pre-ordered Pokemon  games in the series history the Pokemon  company's Chief Operating Officer takato  itsunomiya announced the news at a  launch event for the pair of Pokemon  games though didn't specify how many  pre-orders the games had received he did  note that 440 million units of Pokemon  related games have been sold since the  launch of the very first titles in Japan  Pokemon red and green online the  community seems to be completely divided  on the issue half of the fandom wants  game freak and the Pokemon company to  make improvements and the other half  claims that any technical issues the  games have do not affect their enjoyment  of them personally I find it a little  immersion breaking when characters in an  open world may feat in front of you move  at half the frame rate but maybe that's  just me if you are picking up either of  the new games make sure to grab your  free rare Pikachu once you unlock the  Poke portal in the game which requires  you to start the treasure hunt activity  early on you'll be able to access  mystery gifts like in previous entries  in the series select get via internet  and the Pikachu will be awarded to you  what makes this Pikachu worth obtaining  besides the adorability factor this  particular electric rat knows the move  fly which Pikachu are usually incapable  of learning usually reserved for flying  type Pokemon fly is a useful two-ton  attack that can demolish fighting and  grass type Pokemon on the field adding  some extra utility to this particular  Pikachu this Pikachu will also change  its typing from Electric to Flying when  it is terasterized the new power up  mechanic in the game make sure to head  to gamespot.com for a ton and I do mean  a ton more content around Pokemon  scarlet and violet if you're still in  too deep with Call Of Duty Modern  Warfare 2 and Warzone 2 to care about  pocket monsters and you also to have  Xfinity Internet I hope you haven't paid  for your battle pass yet as you can pick  it up for free members can head to their  rewards and Deals page in their account  and the code should be waiting according  to popular Twitter user that focuses on  all things Call of Duty Charlie Intel as  a reminder the battle pass does away  with the linear nature of previous ones  and instead offers a multi-sector map  players use battle tokens to unlock  items within a certain sector claiming  all items in a sector unlocks the next  one what do you think about the  performance issues in Pokemon Scarlets  and violet let us know in the comments  and we'll see you next time for more  Gamespot news
 

